===Etymology===
{{borrowing|fr|dressage||training|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdɹɛs.ɑːʒ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-uk-dressage.ogg|Audio (UK)|lang=en}}
{{rfp|US|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} the schooling of a horse
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} an [[equestrian]] sport in which the [[horse]] and rider perform a test of specific movements in an arena, and are judged on the horse's obedience, acceptance of the [[bridle]] and of the rider's aids, [[gait]]s, impulsion, and the harmony between horse and rider
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} an event or competition of the sport of dressage
#: ''I'm competing in two dressage shows and a jumping show this weekend''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|the training of a horse}} flatwork, training, haute ecole (high school), classical dressage, {{qualifier|poetically}} ballet on horseback

